@title Real-time quote pricing model architecture
@subtitle Orchard Insurance · ML Platform team · reviewed 2026-10-12

# Overview

The service prices about 450 quotes per second at peak, with a p99 target of 250 ms.

# Architecture diagram

diagram quote dir=LR title="Quote pricing architecture"
quote: portal "Agent Portal" user
quote: gw "API Gateway" lb
quote: modelb "Model Bucket" store
quote: lambda "Inference Lambda" fn
quote: sm "SageMaker Endpoint" svc
quote: fc "Feature Cache" cache
quote: tp "Training Pipeline" svc
quote: mr "Model Registry" store
quote: portal -> gw : quote request
quote: gw -> lambda : invoke
quote: lambda -> fc : get features
quote: lambda -> sm : predict
quote: tp -> mr : register model
quote: mr -> modelb : approved artifact
quote: modelb -> sm : load model
quote: group inf "Inference VPC" lambda, sm, fc
quote: group prod "Prod account" gw, modelb, inf
quote: group ml "ML account" tp, mr

# Capacity

table = Component,Size,Scaling; SageMaker Endpoint,ml.c6i.2xlarge,4 to 12 instances on invocations per instance; Inference Lambda,1024 MB,200 reserved concurrency; Feature Cache,cache.r7g.large,2 replicas

# Deployment

1. Register the model.
2. Approve it in Model Registry.
3. Run a blue/green deploy, shifting 10 percent of traffic every 5 minutes.
4. Roll back automatically if p99 exceeds 250 ms.

!! The Feature Cache is not a source of truth. A cache miss falls back to the policy database and adds about 90 ms.
